      "content": "exactly. it's just math. i look at my bank account and my life expectancy and the numbers just don't add up. i'm spending my entire existence just to service interest. it feels like the only logical way to actually solve the equation is to stop participating entirely. like, if the only outcome is more debt and more exhaustion, why is staying in the game considered the \"right\" thing to do?",
